**Read:** Complete [Design and Manufacturing II — MIT 2.008, 2025](../sources/Design-and-Manufacturing-II-MIT-2025.lingua#r_2FHEWYSEAHBY7X6030TW00F32E)'s available lecture sequence and substantial exercises. Read [Principles and Techniques for Designing Precision Machines — Hale](../sources/Precision-Machine-Design-Hale-Thesis.lingua#r_3V7NVTW0ER7HDK3BJ1HCNPZYN4) progressively as a full advanced text, using its detailed examples after the mechanics, measurement and machine-element foundations.

The three studies linked next extend different parts of the same physical account: how production variation establishes function, how structural and thermal behavior affect useful-point accuracy, and how evidence supports failure and restoration decisions. Shared Records and the same machine may support all three.

**Work:** Complete each investigation with explicit questions, derived predictions, independent evidence, competing explanations and revision. Choose a question that can fail: a process might not produce the expected geometry, a thermal model might not transfer to another history, or a proposed maintenance indicator might track load rather than damage. Preserve the underlying measurements and the limits of their availability.

